In the given C# code, there are four assert statements corresponding to the comments that start with "@@@". The code uses the `Debug.Assert` method to check specific conditions and output an Assert statement.

1. `Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount == Old_arrListLastIndexOfX);` - This statement asserts that the new ArrayList count is the same as the last index of x in the old ArrayList.

2. `Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX > New_arrListIndexOfX);` - This statement asserts that the index of x in the old ArrayList is greater than the index of x in the new ArrayList.

3. `Debug.Assert(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX == New_arrListLastIndexOfX);` - This statement asserts that the last index of x in the old ArrayList is the same as the last index of x in the new ArrayList.

4. `Debug.Assert(!New_arrListContainsX);` - This statement asserts that x does not exist in the new ArrayList. 

